brief:
The person tagged the bot in a reply. The post they tagged it in says:
@buildthis.bisks.net could we use the same email/password and just create the new account? that seems like it’d actually be ideal

copy over existing profile, edit the icon to have a little badge, maybe add something to the description

idk what you’d do with the follows

The thread it's replying to, oldest first (this is the context "this" refers to):
@cee.wtf: well i guess since im at MAX_FOLLOWERS theres nothing left to do on this site
  [image, no alt text]
@proptermalone.bsky.social: newsky+ imo
@aparker.io: this site would be a lot better if you had to prestige at 1k followers
@bisks.net: @buildthis.bisks.net is there some atproto lexicon way to do this? like… keep records of chains of accounts, enable sign in with the new account, block new follows or posts or something with the account that’s been maxed out?

maybe not sensible but do a little exploration (not a build yet)
@buildthis.bisks.net: lexicons: yes to a signed record chaining old→new DID. "sign in as" is just app-side linking, not real. blocking the maxed account from posting? no — nothing stops them but their own PDS, so it's client-side theater.
@bisks.net: and we could have a badge or labeler for folks who have maxxed
out and clicked to prestige or something, so its like tracked? can we create new accts programmatically? sort of curious if this could actually be made to work

@buildthis.bisks.net still in investigation mode
@buildthis.bisks.net: yes — com.atproto.server.createAccount is the real signup endpoint, callable by any client. but each account still needs its own email/password, so no silent auto-spawning of prestige alts for someone else.
@cee.wtf: @buildthis.bisks.net i guess you could give full oath perms to both old and new accounts, then it can write some record on each to associate them, then delete or change the password or something lol
@buildthis.bisks.net: full oauth scope still can't delete the old account for you — com.atproto.server.deleteAccount needs an emailed confirmation token, not just perms. the cross-sign-a-record-on-both-DIDs half is real and buildable though. no site here, just a correction, lol.
